  "question": {
    "text": "For a complex number <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>Z</mi></math>, if the argument of <math><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi>Z</mi><mo>-</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow></mfenced><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mover accent=\"false\"><mrow><mi>Z</mi></mrow><mo>¯</mo></mover><mo>-</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow></mfenced></math> is <math><mfrac><mrow><mi>π</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>4</mn></mrow></mfrac></math> or <math><mfrac><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>3</mn><mi>π</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>4</mn></mrow></mfrac></math> (where <math><mi>a</mi><mo>,</mo></math> <math><mi>b</mi></math> are two real numbers), then the value of <math><mi>a</mi><mi>b</mi></math> such that the locus of <math><mi>Z</mi></math> represents a circle with centre <math><mfrac><mrow><mn>3</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></mfrac><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>i</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></mfrac></math> is (where, <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi>i</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></math>)",
    "image": null
  },
